{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chuanle song\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -Raw 'pipeline/decisions/20260926-160022_route_change.md'; Get-Content -Raw 'pipeline/reviews/motivation_review_20260926-165700.md'; Get-Content -Raw 'pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-G1_native_gate_review_20260925-170100.md'\"","aggregated_output":"# AdaRES_project 决策记录\n\n- **时间**: 2026-09-26 16:00:22\n- **类型**: route_change\n- **问题**: Can mask-interior coherence or local boundary contrast explain B4 selection errors enough to admit one candidate?\n- **决策**: Reject L1 and L2 after native fixed-subset screens; leave server-2 GPU1 vacant and let normal monitor reconcile G1 deathwatch.\n- **依据**: L1 oracle higher 116/240 and standalone mIoU 0.13079; L2 oracle higher 104/240 and standalone mIoU 0.25651 versus B4 subset 0.49186; both fail diagnosis.\n- **证据**: pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-L1-L2_negative_diagnosis_20260926-155700.md; pipeline/research_work.json\n\r\n# Motivation Review - AdaRES_project\n\n2026-09-26 16:57 Asia/Shanghai\n\n## 1. Goal\nGoal: \"AdaRES: improve a faithful standard-indicator 3D referring expression segmentation baseline by learning query confidence from metric-aligned evidence, targeting ScanRefer mIoU >= 0.515.\" B1 0.5020, B4-E30 champion 0.5094, gap 0.0056. Seven goal constraints and three bans apply; server-2 GPUs 0/1 only, one training task per GPU, released backbone and project decoder, no validation hyperparameter scan.\n\n## 2. Story Status\n| Hypothesis | Status | Evidence | Gap |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Competition-aware confidence | Partial | B4-E30 0.5094 | Below target; no fresh seed-matched control |\n| Metric-aligned indicator targets | G1 queue running, deathwatch 2/3 | Targeted log shows Val[30/30] mIoU 0.497 | Monitor terminal reconciliation and best metric |\n| Seed containment | Disconfirmed as stated | M1 oracle higher 48/240 errors | No admission |\n| 2D mask-seed appearance support | Disconfirmed as stated | M2 oracle higher 80/240 errors | No admission |\n\n## 3. Experiment Assessment\nB1 0.5020 establishes baseline. B4-E30 0.5094 is champion. B2-E30 0.5058, C1/C2-E30 0.5008/0.5014, F4 0.5060, D1 0.5080 and H5 0.5061 do not improve it. G1 is not assigned a terminal state from an absent process or the last validation alone. H/J/K/L fixed-cohort screens rejected their specific mechanisms. M1 support-only 0.43714 and M2 appearance-only 0.11752 are below B4 fixed-subset 0.49186.\n\n## 4. Gap Analysis\nThe fixed cohort's oracle mIoU 0.87316 leaves selection headroom but does not establish any usable confidence signal. Full G1 terminal outcome, active queries, latency, peak memory, and subgroup effects remain open. No new candidate passes six hard gates.\n\n## 5. Design Rationale\nM1 asked whether inconsistent mask/seed containment causes B4 errors; M2 asked whether projected 2D appearance can supply independent mask-seed support. Either positive directional signal would have motivated a matched B4 control and candidate-specific backward/resource tests. Both were contradicted on the fixed cohort, so training a renamed feature-fusion or weight variant would not test an evidence-backed mechanism.\n\n## 6. Next Batch\nNo admission. See `pipeline/designs/exp_design_20260926-165700.md`. Resume after normal G1 terminal reconciliation with a new error diagnosis, or independent prospective evidence specifying a stable candidate and native next action.\n\r\n# AdaRES-G1 native gate review\n\n2026-09-25 17:01 Asia/Shanghai. Fixed B4-E30 checkpoint and first 16\nScanRefer validation scenes (441 expressions), then native training pairs on\nserver-2 GPU1. No validation-derived threshold or weight is selected.\n\n| Gate | Evidence | Assessment |\n|---|---|---|\n| Diagnosis | B4 seed/object matched labels disagree with mask quality: among 240 material top-1 errors, 37 selected-positive/oracle-negative pairs. The oracle is positive in 147 errors and the selected query in 54. | Pass as a bounded mismatch; not a causal efficacy claim. |\n| Controls | G1 and B4 configs are byte-identical (SHA256 `1a170434f63da98e10f59c5b17473cde5cf3ff6be0e4381e2771f322853ffa03`); independent package differs only in indicator target computation. | Historical B4-E30 is a fixed 30-epoch continuation control, not a fresh seed-matched run. |\n| Native backward | Target test confirms a high-IoU seed-negative query gets positive gradient and a zero-IoU seed-positive query gets negative gradient; target mask detached. Native [0,1] and [256,257] losses finite with nonzero indicator/decoder gradients. | Pass for tested native batches. |\n| Resources | G1 [0,1] 19.67s, 4.75 GiB reserved; B4 19.63s, 4.75 GiB. G1 [256,257] 24.05s, 6.396 GiB; B4 24.01s, 6.396 GiB. | Pass bounded one-card 24 GiB budget; not worst-case or final throughput. |\n| Independence | G1 changes training indicator target from seed/object membership to detached per-query mask IoU; C1/C2 add listwise/hinge objectives while retaining B4's seed indicator labels, D1 changes rival context, F4 changes decoder neighborhoods. Separate model package and unique config basename. | Distinct causal question, no cross-variant imports. |\n| Constraints | Released backbone, same B4 architecture/config, fresh 30 epochs, only server-2 GPU0/1, single-GPU task, no validation scanning. | Pass. |\n\nNative readouts: [0,1] G1 loss 13.39095, indicator/out_norm gradient\nnorms 3.29086/0.68412, allocated 4.41259 GiB; B4 loss 13.62251,\ngradients 2.47664/0.68415. [256,257] G1 loss 10.86048, gradients\n2.48718/0.91176, allocated 5.87275 GiB; B4 loss 11.08767,\ngradients 1.65840/0.91182. Tests validate mechanism activity, not\ngeneralization or a memory maximum.\n\nThe diagnostic reconstructs seed membership from validation instance labels\nfor analysis only. Training G1's target uses training masks exclusively.\nThe supervision target depends on current mask quality but is stop-gradient,\nso improvement requires learning from changing predictions and could be\nunstable. B4-E30 is not a fresh matched training seed control. Literature\nnovelty and a formal derivation have not been established.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
